eople were together in one  room i mean that's a love thing that's  kind of what it is of course bob  continues to be remembered by fans and  friends alike including fellow comedians  gilbert gottfried margaret cho and  tiffany haddish who all opened up to et  about bob's lasting legacy  the people who knew him will remember  him as you know a great guy  really funny really quick and always  outrageous  and just easy i mean i think that he  will be really seen as somebody who  really  loved comedy as much as he was loved  what a great thing what a great person  he was just so naturally funny naturally  ridiculous and i'll miss him a lot  he's always so motivated so kind  he would send me like tell me proud of  me  send me a message we would cry together  like that's my guy  as for tiffany she got teary-eyed  talking to e.t about the late comedian  explaining that bob was more like family  to her you know i met him when i was 16  when i started the life factory comedy  camp so  um  he was always encouraging and kind and  you know like you know you would watch  tv shows and be like oh where's my dad i  wish i had a dad like that he was like  an instantly like a father figure to me  and then i don't know where like around  the time i turned like 21 22 he shifted  from like a father figure type to a big  brother but that was a beacon for me  that was somebody that was one of those  few people that always encouraged me to  be myself  [Music]

